Based on connect4-alphazero by Eugene Peng:
https://github.com/eugeneyp/connect4-alphazero
Source snapshot: a936aadd74a6a6dd9035e576b89aeb5a3ea7ef73

The inherited game engine, neural network, MCTS, training framework,
configuration, agents, and supporting scripts retain the upstream MIT license.
The pretrained reference checkpoint models/large.pt also comes from that project.

This repository adds the bounded fine-tuning experiments, saved iteration-2
self-play data and checkpoint, training and export checks, standalone inference
improvements, actual-archive comparisons, and their recorded results.

The separate DQN and Double DQN implementation in src/training/double_dqn.py
and scripts/double_dqn.py uses the upstream Connect Four environment and,
for evaluation, its minimax agent. The Q-network, replay and update logic are
implemented directly in PyTorch with Codex assistance. Algorithm references:
Mnih et al., Nature (2015), doi:10.1038/nature14236, and van Hasselt et al.,
AAAI (2016), doi:10.1609/aaai.v30i1.10295.

The move-matched tactical follow-up, alternating multi-step targets, late-game
solver, independent label check and two-ply evaluator are project-specific
additions. They use the inherited board environment, minimax opponent and
window heuristic. The oracle reference test separately loads Peng's pretrained
network and its batched MCTS code.
The experimental training and analysis code and the video renderer were
developed with Codex assistance, as declared in the coursework report.
